const content = `<section><h1>Policy history</h1><p>Hypertext Studio published updated Curfew policies on October 14, 2026. Privacy and Data Retention apply immediately. Updated Terms apply to existing users on November 13, 2026, after 30 days’ notice, and to new users when they sign up or accept them.</p><h2>Current policies</h2><p><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms</a> · <a href="/refund">Refunds</a> · <a href="/retention">Data Retention</a></p><h2>What changed</h2><p>The update identifies the operator, postal address and official legal contact; sets hosted-account eligibility; explains authorized content processing, assistant sharing and task reviews; corrects account deletion and retention descriptions; confirms renewal refunds and offline license treatment; and adds Nevada law and venue with mandatory consumer and home-forum rights preserved. Existing purchases, lifetime licenses, MIT rights and accrued refunds are preserved.</p><h2>Previous documents</h2><p>These are exact copies of the documents in place before publication. The archive label identifies the preceding day; it does not claim that was their original effective date.</p><ul><li><a href="/legal/history/2026-10-13/privacy">Previous Privacy Policy</a></li><li><a href="/legal/history/2026-10-13/terms">Previous Terms</a></li><li><a href="/legal/history/2026-10-13/refund">Previous Refund Policy</a></li><li><a href="/legal/history/2026-10-13/retention">Previous Data Retention Policy</a></li></ul><p>Legal and privacy requests: <a href="mailto:legal@hypertext.studio">legal@hypertext.studio</a>.</p></section>`;
